# $name

A protocol pack for the Deepfake Workbench (`dfwb`): published dataset protocols, meaning
which videos exist, their labels, and exactly how they are split, with no runtime
dependencies of its own. It never contains media, frames, crops, face boxes or anything
derived from pixels.

## Installing

```
pip install $name
```

Installing it registers `$name` with `dfwb` through the `dfwb.plugins` entry point; run
`dfwb protocols list` afterwards to see what it publishes.

## Adding a dataset

Add a directory under `src/$import/packs/<dataset_id>/` holding `dataset.yaml`,
`labels.yaml`, `videos.jsonl.gz`, `splits/*.tsv.gz` and `NOTICE.md`, then list
`<dataset_id>` under `datasets:` in `src/$import/packs/pack.yaml`. Run
`dfwb protocols lint` against the `packs` directory before committing.

